4b. Works cited by the shipped rule and descriptor packs
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are **citations, not licences**. A scientific paper is not a licence: no
permission is needed to implement a published method or to state a published
fact, and no obligation attaches beyond crediting the source - which the packs
and the UI do inline. They are listed here so a reader can find the primary
source for every number.

| Cited work | Where | Note |
|------------|-------|------|
| S. A. Wildman and G. M. Crippen, "Prediction of Physicochemical Parameters by Atomic Contributions", J Chem Inf Comput Sci 1999;39(5):868-873, doi:10.1021/ci990307l | the method implemented by `src/chem/Crippen.cpp`; quoted verbatim as the `citation` field of `assets/packs/descriptors/crippen.json` and returned by `chem::crippenCitation()` | **Citation, not a licence.** The paper describes the method; the BSD-3 obligation in section 4a attaches to the transcribed machine-readable table, not to the method |
| P. Ertl et al., topological polar surface area (fragment-contribution scheme) | `chem::tpsa()` in `src/chem/Descriptors.cpp` | Citation only; the contribution table in the source is a reimplementation of the published scheme |
| Stepan et al. 2011, Chem Res Toxicol 24(9):1345-1410, doi:10.1021/tx200168d | `conceptSource` of `assets/packs/rules/alerts-bioactivation.json` and the `citation` of all 15 alerts | Citation only. No text, table or SMARTS from the paper is reproduced; the SMARTS were authored here |
| 19 distinct primary and reference works cited by the 28 records of `assets/packs/rules/metabolism-facts.json` - including Dring, Smith & Williams (Biochem J 1970;116:425-435), Mitchell et al. (J Pharmacol Exp Ther 1973;187:211-217), de la Torre et al. (Ther Drug Monit 2004;26:137-144), Pennick (Neuropsychiatr Dis Treat 2010;6:317-327), Benowitz, Hukkanen & Jacob (Handb Exp Pharmacol 2009;192:29-60), Thorn et al. PharmGKB caffeine pathway summary (Pharmacogenet Genomics 2012;22:389-395), the CPIC guidelines for CYP2D6/opioids, CYP2D6/atomoxetine and CYP2C9/NSAIDs (Clin Pharmacol Ther 2019-2021), and Goodman & Gilman's *The Pharmacological Basis of Therapeutics*, 13th ed. 2018 | each record's own `citation` field | Citations only - the pack states known biotransformations and names the source of each. Copyrighted text is not reproduced. CPIC's own tables are CC0; PharmGKB / ClinPGx content is CC BY-SA 4.0, so if a future pack copies PharmGKB *content* rather than citing a summary, that pack inherits the share-alike obligation and needs an entry in section 4a |

Attribution and share-alike summary: the weak-copyleft *code* obligation is
Eigen's MPL-2.0. The one third-party *data* licence actually shipped is
BSD-3-Clause, on the transcribed Crippen parameter table and on the Biopython
amino-acid scales, plus CC BY 4.0 on the transcribed IMGT reference and numbering
correspondence (all section 4a) - each notice must travel with any distribution. The share-alike *data* obligation that
can attach is ChEMBL's CC BY-SA 3.0, which today applies to identifiers only.
UniProt (CC BY 4.0) and the curl licence carry attribution obligations.
Everything else above is permissive, public domain, cited rather than copied, or
executed rather than distributed.
